--TEST--
`Core\Db\RolledBack` is a class in spec § 10's tree under `RuntimeError`, and its `reason` is the string it was constructed with — spec § 18, `rule:core-classes/db-transactions`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 18 gives the class one property of its own beyond the root's four, and
// the synthesized constructor fills it from the message: the one string a
// caller passes *is* the reason, so both spellings agree.
try {
    throw new Core\Db\RolledBack("cart is empty");
} catch (Core\Db\RolledBack $e) {
    echo "reason=", $e->reason, "\n";
    echo "message=", $e->message, "\n";
    if ($e->reason == $e->message) {
        echo "same string\n";
    }
}

// It extends `RuntimeError` — a deliberate rollback is the world saying no
// rather than a bug in the program — so every supertype catches it, and
// `LogicError` is not one of them. The clauses are ordered narrow-to-wide so
// the one that matches is the one being asserted.
try {
    throw new Core\Db\RolledBack("deadlock retry gave up");
} catch (LogicError $wrong) {
    echo "not reached: LogicError\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $runtime) {
    echo "runtime=", $runtime->message, "\n";
}

try {
    throw new Core\Db\RolledBack("nothing to commit");
} catch (Throwable $root) {
    echo "root=", $root->message, "\n";
}

// The root's four slots sit at the same indices on every class in the tree,
// so `reason` cannot have displaced one: `previous` still chains and
// `location` still names the throw site rather than the construction site.
var $cause = new IOError("socket closed");
try {
    throw new Core\Db\RolledBack("could not finish", {previous: $cause});
} catch (Core\Db\RolledBack $chained) {
    echo "reason=", $chained->reason, "\n";
    if ($chained->previous is IOError) {
        echo "chained to an IOError\n";
    }
}

// And the property belongs to this class alone: a sibling under the same
// parent is still the root's four and nothing more, which is why the root
// does not pay for a fifth slot on every throw.
try {
    throw new TimeoutError("waited long enough");
} catch (RuntimeError $sibling) {
    echo "sibling=", $sibling->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
reason=cart is empty
message=cart is empty
same string
runtime=deadlock retry gave up
root=nothing to commit
reason=could not finish
chained to an IOError
sibling=waited long enough
